2026-10-14,android,android,P62,ok,n/a,screen,default,"Pixel Tablet AVD (swift-cross-ui-tablet36, API 36, 2560x1600 at 320 dpi), opening p62-doc.txt through the picker. Before: window 2 in the side stage alone (main stage sz=0), bounds 0,0,0,0, window 1 full screen; started on ON_RESUME instead, window 2 took the right half and the left was black. Now started once window 1 has focus again: window 1 left (MAIN), window 2 right (SIDE) with ""original"". Phone re-checked after the change: the picker path and ""new document"" each give a full-screen window, no stageId=SIDE."
2026-10-14,mac,gtk4,P95,ok,n/a,window,default,"Grow mode (SCUI_P95_GROW=1): the mesh view switches between 360 and 720 points wide every 3 s and the window is .contentSize, so the core resizes it through setSize(ofWindow:). p95-mesh.log: drawable 720x600 and 1440x600 alternating, seven changes; eight captures measured with colour_bbox --from-row 110: circle 430x430, ratio 1.000, centred, every time. A resize made by the program redraws the GL area; only a size set through System Events did not."
2026-10-14,android,android,P62,ok,ok,screen,default,"Revoked permission (todo.md P1): saved through CREATE_DOCUMENT into Documents on the device storage (ExternalStorageProvider): ""save -> true"", the file reads AA. Deleted in the Files app: the grant went too (no entry in dumpsys activity permissions). Edited and saved again: ""save -> false"", the write-back logged ""SecurityException: Permission Denial"". In Downloads the same deletion had left the grant."
2026-10-14,mac,appkit,P6,ok,ok,window,default,"macOS sweep 2026-10-14 after the AppKitSynthesiser Command-chord and sRGB colour changes: 121 of 122 files pass (replayed + captured + exit 0, not each file's assertions). P6-transport-toggles is the one fail, capture=fail, and it is the environment: P6 autoplays from ~/proj/LZFSE2/swift_tar/images, which exists neither on this Mac nor on the Mac mini, so no frame is presented, the render marker never comes and the only capture is named -timeout-. The replay itself completed."
