2026-10-15,mac,gtk4,P88,ok,ok,window,default,"Touch-hold hover on GtkBackend (queue item 10), measured with the mouse standing in for a finger: a build with touch-only off and the motion controller silenced, so only the hold path could report. First try, GestureLongPress + GestureDrag: the hold reported once (hover reports 1, panel orange) and nothing after, because the panel's own drag claimed the sequence and GTK cancelled the second drag. Second, GestureLongPress + an EventControllerLegacy in the capture phase: press, 1 s, two moves, lift gives ""hover reports: 23"", ""last active: x=180 y=142"" (the motion path maps the same window point the same way), ""pointer: ended"", ""drags: 1"". Screen frames during a held press (frames_during.zsh, mac): panel orange with ""pointer: x=180 y=142"" in 8 of 30. The shipped build is touch-only again; with it the normal P88 file still gives ""pointer: x=160 y=102"", cmd 130,122, drags 1. No touch screen here, so a real GDK_TOUCH_* sequence is not yet measured."
2026-10-15,ios,uikit,P88,ok,ok,window,default,"iPhone 17 simulator, the panel during a held finger, captured from outside the runner (frames_during.zsh with simctl io screenshot): an XCUITest press of 3 s on the panel; frames 10-18 of 30 show the whole panel orange (1080x720 px) with ""pointer: x=104 y=90"" and ""hover reports: 1"", blue before and after. Run twice, 9 orange frames each time."
