2026-10-19,mac,appkit,P108,ok,ok,window,default,"inertialDrag(offset:bounds:) (debug build with SCUI_DEBUG in the package's own .build, test.zsh -n --actionfile actions/mac/P108-throw.actions): FREE fling 400 pt/s, coast frames on the closed form err 0.0000 pt over 228 frames, end 199.80 (400*0.4995), 3.800 s (closed form 3.796), 60 frames/s; BOUND fling 3000 pt/s stops on the bound, max 300.00, end 300.00, 0.817 s; real THROW: release velocity 180.2 pt/s against 180.3 over the last 0.1 s of the received points (received every 20.5 ms), coast err 0.0000 over 204 frames, end 139.99 = release + v*tau; HOLD: the card picked up where the throw left it, moved 20 pt, release velocity 0, no coast. Found and fixed: AppKitHitTestingContainer hit-tested a geometric-effect container at its layout frame and refused points outside its parent, so the thrown card could only be picked up at its layout position."
2026-10-19,mac,gtk4,P108,ok,ok,window,default,"inertialDrag on GtkBackend (macOS, debug build with SCUI_DEBUG in the package's own .build, test.zsh -n --actionfile actions/mac/P108-throw-gtk4.actions): FREE err 0.0000 over 227 frames, end 199.80, 3.801 s; BOUND end 300.00, 0.815 s; real THROW release 205.3 pt/s against 205.7 over the last 0.1 s (points every 17.6 ms), coast err 0.0000 over 207 frames, end 152.54 = release + v*tau; HOLD picked up where it was left, release velocity 0, no coast. Found and fixed: after an animation ended, the next GTK frame clock start gave its first tick 1.5-4.2 s late (end_updating then begin_updating with nothing invalidated); a 60 Hz main-queue tick now runs until the first clock tick, first tick 0.05 s after the second fling."
2026-10-19,mac,appkit,P109,ok,n/a,window,default,"Text foregroundColor/foregroundStyle and Linear/Radial/Angular gradients tween (debug build in the package's own .build, test.zsh -n): WITH MID p=0.517, values handed to the backend against closed forms: colour err 0.0 (0-255) and location/point/radius/angle err 0.000 for both texts and all three gradients (same stops, different stops resampled, points, radius 20->60, angle 0->90 degrees); 62-63 frames in 1 s; root body evaluations 1 by the middle; DONE 1.04 s at the end values; JUMP one sample each. A mid-flight window capture shows the purple text and all three gradients in between. Found and fixed: AppKit's LinearGradientView and RadialGradientView redrew only on a size change, so a changed gradient at the same size stayed drawn as before (UIKit's views and Android's GradientWidget had the same shape and got the same fix, not run)."
2026-10-19,mac,gtk4,P109,ok,n/a,window,default,"Text colour and gradient tweens on GtkBackend (macOS, debug build in the package's own .build, test.zsh -n with TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): WITH MID p=0.515 colour err 0.0, other err 0.000 for both texts and three gradients; 56-57 frames in 1 s; body evaluations 1 by the middle; DONE 1.01 s; JUMP one sample each. A mid-flight window capture shows the text and gradients in between."
