2026-10-19,windows,winui,P39,ok,ok,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1, test.zsh -win --no-build --showtime 5 with actions/win/P39-read-nine-cells-against-the-control.actions, rc=0. grayscale is now AppKit's linear-light grey (decode, luminance, overlay against 0.5 grey, encode; a tree of Win2D effects, one copy of the upstream per branch): grayscale 1 within 2 levels of the formula at 10 points; grayscale 0.5, by a temporary edit, within 2 at 8 points. Contrast as in the earlier row."
2026-10-19,windows,winui,P102,ok,ok,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1, test.zsh -win --no-build --showtime 12 with actions/win/P102-long-press-drag.actions, 33 actions, rc=0. p102-select.log: FIELD began 6..<6 '' then ended forward 6..<30 'ick brown fox jumps over' after 3 changes; EDITOR began 88..<88 then ended backward 2..<88; no line for the CONTROL long press or the quick 0.1 s FIELD drag. First run of WinUI's LongPressTextSelection (GetRectFromCharacterIndex in LongPressTextBox)."
2026-10-19,windows,winui,P66,ok,ok,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1, idle. SAMPLES 27 over 0.62s, monotonic (26 on a second run; 20 while a build ran); macOS AppKit 31. Was 2 idle: DispatchQueue.main was drained only by the run-loop tickler, whose SetTimer was re-armed by every window message and so never fired during an animation. Now the tickler keeps an earlier timer and waits on libdispatch's main-queue handle, draining with _dispatch_main_queue_callback_4CF. Idle CPU unchanged against SCUI_WINUI_MTA=1."
2026-10-19,windows,gtk4,P66,ok,ok,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1. SAMPLES 7 over 0.62s through test.zsh, monotonic (was 2 idle); macOS GTK 26. GtkCHelpers now watches libdispatch's main-queue handle (Windows: a one-shot thread-pool wait handing the drain to g_idle_add_full; Linux: g_unix_fd_add on the eventfd, as AndroidBackend does). See the GPU row below for the rest of the gap."
2026-10-19,windows,winui,P47,ok,ok,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1, actions/win/P47-draw-every-symbol.actions. The last label now reads 'unknown' whole (was 'unkno...'): measured text width is rounded up plus one DIP, because layout rounding at 125% left a TextBlock a fraction of a DIP short and .characterEllipsis trimmed it. Rounding up alone did not cure it."
2026-10-19,windows,winui,P102,ok,ok,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1. With the text-width fix the label reads 'EDITOR (long press, then drag)' whole (was 'EDITOR (long press, then...'). Selection behaviour as in the earlier row."
