2026-10-19,windows,winui,P92,ok,partial,window,default,"Swift 6.4.1, SCUI_P92_MENU=1, window now 640 wide so all menus show (both modes measured by UIA). The user, by hand, on the menu bar: Edit > Paste wrote 'field hellohello' and Edit > Undo 'field hello' in p92-commands.log -- WinUIBackend+StandardCommands.swift acts on the text box remembered through FocusManager.gotFocus. Standard items sit with the CommandGroup(after:) items beside them (UIA). Synthetic input: the first menu item pressed per launch runs (press and release 0.12 s apart; a plain click closes the menu without running it), later ones do not -- open, so no actions/win file yet. Win32Synthesiser no longer takes a WinUI PopupWindowSiteBridge for a modal."
