2026-10-19,mac,gtk4,P96,ok,n/a,window,default,"GTK frame clock at the display rate. Cause measured with testapp/test_support/measure/gtk_frame_trace.c (DYLD-injected): GDK 4.24 stops its CVDisplayLink after every presented frame and starts it from the next paint (498 ticks, 498 starts, 497 stops in one run); a start made 0-10 ms before the next callback slot got its first callback one refresh late (0 on time / 147 late), 12-18 ms before it was on time (95 / 2), while tick to start took a median 3-4 ms. GtkBackend now keeps GDK's display link running while its frame clock runs (scui_macos_display_link_keep_running, GtkCHelpers/gtk_display_link_macos.c). Ticks per 3 s, before: FRAMES 103/100/103 (33.3-34.3 fps), FRAMES-ALONE 173/169/174 (56.3-58.0 fps); after: FRAMES 177/177/176 (58.7-59.0 fps), FRAMES-ALONE 180/180/180 (60.0 fps), every tick interval one refresh in the trace. Curve err 0.000 pt and x err 0.000 at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5 s in all six runs. The link stops again when the frame clock stops (no callbacks once idle)."
2026-10-19,mac,gtk4,P104,ok,n/a,window,default,"Same change (GDK's display link kept running while the frame clock runs). WITH frames before: 58/35/33; after: 61/61/60/61 (DONE at 1.00-1.02 s, err 0.00 pt, colour err 0.0). The row 30 claim that several re-layouts per frame held WITH to 32 frames is not what the trace shows: tick to after-paint in the WITH second is median 3.1 ms, max 5.2 ms, none over 16.7 ms; the missing frames were the display link restart. VALUE after: err 0.71-1.60 pt over 60-61 frames (limit 3, before 0.15-1.32 over 59-60); JUMP 1 sample."
