2026-10-19,mac,gtk4,P105,ok,n/a,window,default,"Default transition on GtkBackend (macOS, debug build in the worktree's own .build, test.zsh -n with TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): DEFAULT IF insert MID p=0.500 opacity err 0.000, DONE 1.00 s; remove MID p=0.517 err 0.000, onDisappear 1.01 s; ELSE MID p=0.521 err 0.000 both; EACH remove p=0.521 (clock 0.505) err 0.000, insert p=0.500 (clock 0.495) err 0.000; NOANIM frames 0; IDENTITY 76 frames all opacity 1. Mid-removal capture: the row fades at its old position. Explicit transitions unchanged (err 0.00/0.000). In one run the first step (INSERT) took 14.7 s with 4 frames (the GTK frame clock started late for the first animation of the app); the other complete run gave INSERT DONE 1.03 s. P100 err 0.00 on the same build."
2026-10-19,mac,appkit,P110,ok,n/a,window,default,"Gradients that tween (debug build in the worktree's own .build, test.zsh -n): WITH MID p=0.517, values handed to the backend against closed forms, colour err 0.0/255 and point/radius err 0.000 for Text .foregroundStyle linear->linear (tg) and flat blue->linear (tc), Circle .fill linear->linear, RoundedRectangle flat->radial, Circle .stroke gradient, unfilled Capsule under .foregroundStyle; DONE 1.03 s at the end values, 61-62 frames each; VALUE (.animation(value:)) Text and Rectangle p=0.500 (clock 0.507) err 0.0/0.000, 50 frames; JUMP one sample each at the start values; FINAL err 0. Final and mid-flight captures show gradient-filled text (red to blue, red to green) and the shapes in their gradients. P109, P104 and P43 re-run on the same build: P109 err 0.0/0.000, P104 WITH err 0.00 pt colour 0.0, VALUE 0.94 pt (pass <= 3), P43 shapes drawn clipped as before."
